From cb4e51dd913c4f187d69388123ab8c5188798fac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dave Seddon <dave.seddon.ca@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 27 May 2026 16:37:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH RFC 1/3] net: flow_dissector: add opt-in fast-path entry-point
 skeleton

Add a fast-path dispatcher to __skb_flow_dissect(), gated by the
new net.core.flow_dissector_fastpath sysctl. It runs after the BPF
flow_dissector check and before the slow-path graph walk.

The gate uses a static_branch at the call site:

    if (static_branch_likely(&flow_dissector_fastpath_key) &&
        flow_dissect_fast(skb, ...))
            return true;

Default off. We use static_branch_likely (not _unlikely) because
operators who flip this sysctl have opted into the fast-path for
performance; static_branch_likely keeps the dispatcher inline in
the hot text section so they get the layout the microbench
measured against. The trade is one forward JMP per dissector call
in the default-off case (cheap, one not-taken JMP) versus a
cold-section detour per call in the enabled case if we had used
_unlikely.

The sysctl uses proc_do_static_key, the canonical helper for
sysctl-toggled static_branches (cf. net.core.high_order_alloc_disable
in net/core/sysctl_net_core.c, sock.c:net_high_order_alloc_disable_key).

The dispatcher checks three conditions before doing any work:

- The caller must use flow_keys_dissector or
  flow_keys_dissector_symmetric. Custom dissectors (e.g. tc
  cls_flow with bespoke key sets) fall back to the slow path.
- The flags must be empty or only FLOW_DISSECTOR_F_PARSE_1ST_FRAG.
  Other flags request behaviour this code does not implement
  (encap walking, MPLS deep parse, flow-label stop).
- The outer ethertype must be IPv4 or IPv6.

If all three conditions hold the dispatcher calls a per-shape
helper. Other cases return false and the slow path runs as before.

The per-shape helpers (flow_dissect_fast_ipv4,
flow_dissect_fast_ipv6) are added as stubs that return false. Real
bodies arrive in follow-up patches.

This patch does not change behaviour:

- Default sysctl value is 0; the static_branch stays false and the
  static_branch_likely test is patched to skip the dispatcher.
- Even with the sysctl set to 1, every fast-path stub returns
  false in this patch alone, so every packet still reaches the
  slow path.
- Added cost is one not-taken JMP per dissector call when disabled
  (the default), and one ethertype switch (about 5 cycles) per
  call that passes the BPF override check when enabled.

The framework patch is sent on its own so reviewers can comment on
the dispatch shape, the dissector identity check, the BPF order,
and the sysctl-gating design separately from the per-shape
extractor code.

Signed-off-by: Dave Seddon <dave.seddon.ca@gmail.com>
